          "title": "Big Picture & Simple Concepts",
          "markdown": "![Source Transformation, Mesh/Nodal Circuit and Star-Delta](/notes/diagrams/u1-dc-mesh-nodal-stardelta.svg)\n\n\n## 1. Big Picture & Simple Concepts\n\nEvery electrical circuit moves electric charge (**current $I$**) pushed by potential difference (**voltage $V$**):\n1. **Circuit Elements ($R, L, C$):**\n   - **Resistor ($R$, Ohms $\\Omega$):** Opposes current and turns energy into heat ($P = I^2R$). Always **passive**, **linear**, and **bilateral**.\n   - **Inductor ($L$, Henry $\\text{H}$):** Coiled wire storing energy in a **magnetic field** ($E = \\frac{1}{2}LI^2$, $v = L\\frac{di}{dt}$). Opposes sudden current change; acts as a **short circuit** to steady DC.\n   - **Capacitor ($C$, Farad $\\text{F}$):** Parallel plates storing energy in an **electric field** ($E = \\frac{1}{2}CV^2$, $i = C\\frac{dv}{dt}$). Opposes sudden voltage change; acts as an **open circuit** to steady DC.\n2. **Classification of Elements:**\n   - **Active vs Passive:** *Active* supplies net energy (batteries, generators, op-amps, transistors); *Passive* absorbs, dissipates, or stores energy ($R, L, C$).\n   - **Unilateral vs Bilateral:** *Bilateral* conducts equally in both directions ($R, L, C$); *Unilateral* conducts differently when polarity reverses (diode, BJT).\n   - **Linear vs Non-linear:** *Linear* obeys **homogeneity** and **superposition** ($V = IR$ straight line through origin); *Non-linear* curves (diode, thermistor, electric arc).\n   - **Lumped vs Distributed:** *Lumped* elements sit at discrete points ($R,L,C$); *Distributed* parameters spread along length (transmission lines).\n3. **Sources:**\n   - **Ideal Voltage Source:** Constant $V$ at all currents ($R_{\\text{int}} = 0$). **Practical Voltage Source:** $V$ in series with small $R_s$, terminal $V_L = V - I R_s$.\n   - **Ideal Current Source:** Constant $I$ at all voltages ($R_{\\text{int}} = \\infty$). **Practical Current Source:** $I$ in parallel with large $R_p$.\n4. **Core Laws:**\n   - **Ohm's Law:** $V = IR$ at constant temperature (fails for non-linear diodes/transistors).\n   - **KCL (Kirchhoff's Current Law):** Based on **conservation of charge**; $\\sum I_{\\text{in}} = \\sum I_{\\text{out}}$ at any node.\n   - **KVL (Kirchhoff's Voltage Law):** Based on **conservation of energy**; $\\sum V_{\\text{rise}} - \\sum V_{\\text{drop}} = 0$ around any closed loop."
