          "number": "2",
          "title": "Step-by-Step Analysis Methods",
          "markdown": "## 2. Step-by-Step Analysis Methods\n\n### Method A: Source Transformation\n* Converting a voltage source ($V_s$ in series with $R_s$) into a current source ($I_s$ in parallel with $R_s$):\n  $$\\boxed{I_s = \\frac{V_s}{R_s}}, \\qquad R_{\\text{parallel}} = R_s$$\n* Converting current source ($I_s \\parallel R_p$) into voltage source ($V_s$ series $R_p$): $\\boxed{V_s = I_s R_p}$. *(Arrows point toward the `+` terminal!)*\n\n### Method B: Mesh Analysis (Using KVL)\n1. Identify every **mesh** (smallest loop containing no inner loops). Assign clockwise mesh currents $I_1, I_2, \\dots$\n2. **Note on Current Sources:** You **cannot apply KVL directly across a current source** (its terminal voltage is unknown!).\n   - If a current source sits on an outer branch, that mesh current is fixed immediately ($I_k = \\pm I_s$).\n   - If a current source is shared between two meshes $a$ and $b$, skip the shared branch and apply KVL around the outer **supermesh**, plus add the constraint equation relating $I_a - I_b = I_s$.\n3. Apply KVL ($\\sum \\text{drops} = \\sum \\text{rises}$) around each mesh.\n4. Solve the simultaneous linear equations to obtain branch currents.\n\n### Method C: Nodal Analysis (Using KCL)\n1. Count essential nodes ($3+$ branches meeting). Pick one (usually bottom ground rail) as **reference node ($V = 0\\text{ V}$)** and label unknown node voltages $V_A, V_B, \\dots$\n2. Apply KCL ($\\sum I_{\\text{leaving}} = \\sum I_{\\text{entering}}$) at each non-reference node using $I = \\frac{V_{\\text{high}} - V_{\\text{low}}}{R}$.\n3. *(If a voltage source connects two non-reference nodes, enclose both in a **supernode**.)*\n4. Solve simultaneous equations for node voltages, then compute every branch current.\n\n### Method D: Star ($\\text{Y}$) $\\leftrightarrow$ Delta ($\\Delta$) Transformation\n* **Delta to Star ($\\Delta \\to \\text{Y}$):** Each Star arm equals the product of the two **adjacent** Delta arms divided by the sum of all three Delta arms:\n  $$\\boxed{R_1 = \\frac{R_{12} R_{13}}{R_{12} + R_{23} + R_{13}}}, \\quad R_2 = \\frac{R_{12} R_{23}}{R_{12} + R_{23} + R_{13}}, \\quad R_3 = \\frac{R_{13} R_{23}}{R_{12} + R_{23} + R_{13}}$$\n* **Star to Delta ($\\text{Y} \\to \\Delta$):** Each Delta arm equals the sum of all pairwise Star products divided by the **opposite** Star arm:\n  $$\\boxed{R_{12} = \\frac{R_1 R_2 + R_2 R_3 + R_3 R_1}{R_3}}, \\quad R_{23} = \\frac{\\sum R_i R_j}{R_1}, \\quad R_{13} = \\frac{\\sum R_i R_j}{R_2}$$\n* **Balanced Shortcut ($R_{12}=R_{23}=R_{13}=R_\\Delta$ and $R_1=R_2=R_3=R_Y$):** $\\boxed{R_\\Delta = 3 R_Y}$ or $\\boxed{R_Y = R_\\Delta / 3}$."
