          "markdown": "## 6. Common Mistakes Checklist\n* Applying **Ohm's law** or **Star–Delta** carelessly to non-linear devices like diodes or ignoring battery polarity (`+` vs `-`) in KVL.\n* Using the **wrong resistor in the numerator** of Current Divider Rule: $I_1 = I \\frac{\\mathbf{R_2}}{R_1 + R_2}$ (opposite resistor goes on top!), unlike Voltage Divider $V_1 = V \\frac{R_1}{R_1 + R_2}$.\n* Attempting to write a KVL equation *through* an ideal current source without creating a **supermesh**.\n* Swapping $\\Delta \\to \\text{Y}$ vs $\\text{Y} \\to \\Delta$ ratios: remember $\\mathbf{R_\\Delta = 3 R_Y}$ (Delta is always larger for equal resistances!).\n* Forgetting sign inversion in a **shared branch** between Mesh 1 ($I_1$) and Mesh 2 ($I_2$): Mesh 1 sees $R(I_1 - I_2)$ when both loops are chosen clockwise."
