          "title": "Exam Questions (With Complete Answers)",
          "markdown": "## 5. Exam Questions (With Complete Answers)\n\n### Short Answer Questions (2 Marks Each)\n\n1. **Define Form Factor and Peak Factor and state their sinusoidal values.**\n   **Answer:** *Form factor* $k_f = V_{\\text{rms}}/V_{\\text{avg}} = 1.11$ (sine wave); *Peak factor* $k_p = V_m/V_{\\text{rms}} = \\sqrt{2} = 1.414$.\n2. **What is the average power consumed by a pure inductor or pure capacitor?**\n   **Answer:** **Zero** ($\\cos(\\pm 90^\\circ) = 0$). Pure $L$ and $C$ borrow energy during one quarter-cycle and return the exact same energy during the next quarter-cycle.\n3. **Define Impedance and Admittance with SI units.** *(BEU 2026)*\n   **Answer:** *Impedance* $Z = R + jX$ ($\\Omega$) is total AC opposition to current; *Admittance* $Y = 1/Z = G + jB$ ($\\text{Siemens, S}$) measures how easily AC flows.\n4. **Why is low power factor bad for power systems, and how do we improve it?**\n   **Answer:** At fixed real power $P$, low $\\cos\\phi$ forces higher current $I = P/(V\\cos\\phi)$, raising $I^2R$ cable heat losses and transformer kVA cost. Adding **shunt capacitor banks** across inductive loads supplies local reactive VARs and boosts $\\cos\\phi$.\n5. **State three advantages of a 3-phase AC system over single-phase.**\n   **Answer:** (i) Instantaneous total power is constant (smooth motor torque, less vibration); (ii) requires less conductor copper for the same power transfer; (iii) gives both $400\\text{ V}$ line and $230\\text{ V}$ domestic voltages cleanly.\n\n### Long Answer Questions (7–10 Marks Each)\n\n1. **Derive the expressions for Average value, RMS value, Form Factor ($1.11$), and Peak Factor ($\\sqrt{2}$) of a sinusoidal AC waveform.** *(Follow §2.1 step-by-step integration + the AC Circuits diagram above, part (a).)*\n2. **Derive the line-to-phase voltage and current relations in 3-phase Star ($V_L = \\sqrt{3}V_{\\text{ph}}$) and Delta ($I_L = \\sqrt{3}I_{\\text{ph}}$) connections, and show total power $P = \\sqrt{3}V_L I_L\\cos\\phi$.** *(Follow §2.4 + the AC Circuits diagram above, part (c).)*\n3. **Explain series $R\\text{–}L\\text{–}C$ AC circuit analysis with phasor diagram, impedance triangle, power triangle, and resonance. Solve a numerical on $P, Q, S,$ and $\\cos\\phi$.** *(Follow §2.3 + the AC Circuits diagram above, part (b).)*"
