          "id": "ch-6-common-mistakes-checklist",
          "number": "6",
          "title": "Common Mistakes Checklist",
          "markdown": "## 6. Common Mistakes Checklist\n* Using **peak voltage $V_m$** instead of **RMS voltage $V$** in $P = VI\\cos\\phi$ ($230\\text{ V}$ wall/spec voltage is ALWAYS RMS unless a formula $V_m\\sin\\omega t$ is given!).\n* Writing $X_C = 2\\pi f C$ instead of $\\frac{1}{2\\pi f C}$, or forgetting to convert $\\mu\\text{F} \\to 10^{-6}\\text{ F}$ and $\\text{mH} \\to 10^{-3}\\text{ H}$.\n* Plugging **$V_L$ directly** across one phase of a **Star-connected** load: in Star, $V_{\\text{ph}} = V_L / \\sqrt{3}$!\n* Using $3 V_L I_L \\cos\\phi$ instead of **$\\sqrt{3} V_L I_L \\cos\\phi$** (the $3$ factor belongs to $3 V_{\\text{ph}} I_{\\text{ph}}\\cos\\phi$!).\n* Adding impedances $Z = R + jX$ magnitudes arithmetically ($R + X_L$) instead of vectorially ($\\sqrt{R^2 + (X_L - X_C)^2}$)."
