          "id": "ch-6-common-mistakes-checklist",
          "number": "6",
          "title": "Common Mistakes Checklist",
          "markdown": "## 6. Common Mistakes Checklist\n* Using **$\\Phi_{\\text{rms}}$** or plugging $\\text{mWb}$ directly without converting to $\\text{Wb}$ ($\\times 10^{-3}$) into $E = 4.44 f N \\Phi_m$.\n* Referring secondary impedance to primary with $K$ instead of **$1/K^2 = (N_1/N_2)^2$** (impedance scales as turns ratio **squared**!).\n* Forgetting $x^2$ on copper loss at fractional load ($P_{cu}(x) = x^2 P_{cu,\\text{fl}}$, NOT $x P_{cu,\\text{fl}}$, because $P \\propto I^2$).\n* Swapping **Lap ($A = P$)** and **Wave ($A = 2$)** parallel paths in DC machine calculations, or forgetting $I_a = I_L - I_{sh}$ for a shunt motor.\n* Computing rotor frequency as $f_r = (1 - s)f$ instead of **$f_r = s f$**."
