          "id": "ch-6-number-base-conversions-complement-arithmetic",
          "number": "6",
          "title": "Number Base Conversions & Complement Arithmetic",
          "markdown": "## 6. Number Base Conversions & Complement Arithmetic\n\n| Number System | Base ($r$) | Digits | Bit Grouping Shortcut |\n| :--- | :---: | :--- | :--- |\n| **Binary** | $2$ | $0, 1$ | Base representation |\n| **Octal** | $8$ | $0\\text{–}7$ | $3$ binary bits per octal digit |\n| **Decimal** | $10$ | $0\\text{–}9$ | Standard human base |\n| **Hexadecimal** | $16$ | $0\\text{–}9, A(10), B(11), C(12), D(13), E(14), F(15)$ | $4$ binary bits per hex digit |\n\n### Conversion Rules\n1. **Any Base $r \\to$ Decimal:** Expand weights around the radix point: $\\sum d_i \\cdot r^i$ (example: $(10010.101)_2 = 16 + 2 + 0.5 + 0.125 = 18.625_{10}$).\n2. **Decimal $\\to$ Base $r$:**\n   * **Integer part:** Repeatedly divide by $r$ and read remainders **bottom-to-top** (example: $63_{10} = 111111_2$).\n   * **Fractional part:** Repeatedly multiply fraction by $r$ and read integer carries **top-to-bottom** (example: $0.25_{10} = .01_2$, so $(63.25)_{10} = (111111.01)_2$).\n3. **Binary $\\leftrightarrow$ Octal / Hex:** Group bits outward from the radix point in **$3$s (Octal)** or **$4$s (Hex)**, padding zeros at outer ends (example: $(\\text{A6B.0F})_{16} = 1010\\,0110\\,1011\\,.\\,0000\\,1111_2 = (5153.036)_8$).\n4. **2's Complement Subtraction ($A - B$ in $n$ bits):**\n   * Take **1's complement** of $B$ (flip bits) and add $1$ to get **2's complement**.\n   * Compute $A + (\\text{2's comp of } B)$. If carry-out $= 1$, discard carry (positive answer). If carry-out $= 0$, answer is negative; take 2's complement of sum and prefix a minus sign."
